# Privacy Policy

**Last updated: 29 September 2026**

Bergmeijer ICT respects your privacy and handles personal data with care. This privacy policy explains what personal data may be collected when you visit **[www.bergmeijer-ict.com](http://www.bergmeijer-ict.com)**, why it is used, and what rights you have under the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR/AVG).

## 1. Who we are

**Bergmeijer ICT**
Website: https://www.bergmeijer-ict.com
Email: [info@bergmeijer-ict.com](mailto:info@bergmeijer-ict.com)
Telephone: +31 6 29097171

For privacy-related questions or requests concerning your personal data, please contact us using the email address above.

## 2. What personal data we process

Depending on how you use the website, we may process the following personal data:

* Name
* Email address
* Telephone number, if you provide it
* The subject of your message
* The contents of your message
* Technical information that is automatically transmitted when you visit the website, such as IP address, browser type and operating system, where this information is processed by the website or its hosting infrastructure.

We only request or process personal data that is relevant for the applicable purpose.

## 3. Contact form

If you use the contact form on the website, we process the information you provide in order to:

* receive and respond to your enquiry;
* communicate with you about your enquiry;
* take any necessary steps before entering into an agreement, where applicable.

Providing information through the contact form is voluntary. However, without the information necessary to identify you and respond to your request, we may not be able to answer your enquiry.

## 4. Legal basis

Depending on the circumstances, personal data may be processed on one or more of the following legal bases under the GDPR:

* **Consent** — where you have given permission for a specific processing activity.
* **Legitimate interest** — where processing is necessary for legitimate business purposes and your interests or fundamental rights do not override those interests.
* **Contract or pre-contractual measures** — where processing is necessary to perform a contract or to take steps at your request before entering into a contract.
* **Legal obligation** — where processing is necessary to comply with a legal obligation.

We do not use personal data for purposes that are incompatible with the purpose for which it was collected.

## 5. How long we retain personal data

We do not retain personal data longer than necessary for the purpose for which it was collected, unless a longer retention period is required by law.

The appropriate retention period depends on the nature of the information and the reason why it was collected. For example, information relating to an enquiry may be retained for as long as reasonably necessary to handle the enquiry and any resulting business relationship.

Where legal or financial records are subject to statutory retention requirements, those requirements take precedence.

## 6. Sharing personal data with third parties

We do not sell your personal data.

Personal data may be processed by service providers where this is necessary to operate the website or provide services. Such parties may include providers of:

* website hosting;
* email services;
* website security and technical infrastructure;
* other services that are necessary to operate the website.

Where required by the GDPR, appropriate agreements and safeguards are used when third parties process personal data on our behalf.

## 7. International transfers

If a service provider processes personal data outside the European Economic Area (EEA), we will ensure that the transfer is carried out in accordance with applicable GDPR requirements.

This may include an adequacy decision, Standard Contractual Clauses or another legally recognised transfer mechanism.

## 8. Cookies

The website may use cookies and similar technologies.

### Necessary cookies

Some cookies may be necessary for the website to function correctly, maintain security, or provide functionality requested by the visitor.

### Analytics and other cookies

If analytical, tracking or other non-essential cookies are used, the applicable cookie information and consent mechanism will be provided on the website.

Non-essential cookies that require consent will only be placed after the required consent has been obtained.

You can manage cookies through your browser settings and, where applicable, through the website's cookie-consent mechanism.

Dutch rules require visitors to be informed about cookies and, for certain types of cookies such as tracking cookies, require consent before those cookies are placed.

## 9. Website security

We take reasonable technical and organisational measures to protect personal data against unauthorised access, loss, alteration or disclosure.

However, no internet transmission or storage system can be guaranteed to be completely secure.

## 10. Your privacy rights

Under the GDPR, you may have the following rights:

* the right to access your personal data;
* the right to correct inaccurate or incomplete personal data;
* the right to request deletion of personal data;
* the right to restrict processing;
* the right to object to certain processing;
* the right to data portability, where applicable;
* the right to withdraw consent where processing is based on consent.

To exercise your rights, contact us at:

**[info@bergmeijer-ict.com](mailto:info@bergmeijer-ict.com)**

Please provide enough information for us to identify your request. We may need to verify your identity before providing personal data or making changes.

We will respond to requests within the period required by applicable privacy legislation.

## 11. Complaints

If you have a complaint about how your personal data is handled, we would appreciate the opportunity to resolve the issue first. Please contact us at:

**[info@bergmeijer-ict.com](mailto:info@bergmeijer-ict.com)**

You also have the right to lodge a complaint with the Dutch Data Protection Authority (**Autoriteit Persoonsgegevens**).

## 12. Children's privacy

This website is not specifically directed at children. We do not knowingly collect personal data from children through the website for purposes that require parental consent.

## 13. Changes to this privacy policy

We may update this privacy policy when the website, our services or applicable privacy requirements change.

The latest version will always be published on this page. The date at the top of this policy indicates when it was last updated.

## 14. Contact

If you have questions about this privacy policy or about the processing of your personal data, please contact:

